# Answer key for B11 t2_scd2.sql - integration: an SCD2 dimension.
#
# WRITTEN FROM SOURCE BEFORE THE ANALYSER WAS RUN OVER THIS FILE.
# Conventions: every decision D-1..D-44. The temp table is pg_temp.chg (D-31); variables
# are `var:<name>`, bands per edge (B8 rule 5).

@ 18 S1 the changed customers
value staging.customers.id -> pg_temp.chg.id identity
value staging.customers.email -> pg_temp.chg.email identity
value staging.customers.full_name -> pg_temp.chg.full_name identity
value staging.customers.country_code -> pg_temp.chg.country_code identity
value staging.customers.segment -> pg_temp.chg.segment identity
filter staging.customers.status, staging.customers.created_at -> pg_temp.chg
filter core.dim_customer.valid_from -> pg_temp.chg post
note A subquery compared in WHERE decides which rows land: its column is a filter (B2), and valid_from reaches the comparison through MAX: post-aggregation, per column (D-6; B2 T1's AVG precedent).

@ 28 S2 close out the current versions
filter core.dim_customer.is_current -> core.dim_customer
note d.customer_id = c.id joins the FROM relation to the target: structural (D-11, B3). SET writes literals.

@ 39 S3 insert the new versions
value pg_temp.chg.id -> core.dim_customer.customer_id identity
value pg_temp.chg.email -> core.dim_customer.email derived
value pg_temp.chg.full_name -> core.dim_customer.full_name identity
value pg_temp.chg.country_code -> core.dim_customer.country_code identity
value pg_temp.chg.segment -> core.dim_customer.segment identity
value core.dim_store.region -> core.dim_customer.region identity
value core.dim_store.country_code, pg_temp.chg.country_code -> core.dim_customer.region conditional
influence core.dim_store.opened_on -> core.dim_customer.region
note The lookup's projected column passes through (B2-01); its WHERE, both correlation operands, is a conditional value (D-12); its ORDER BY ... LIMIT 1 is influence (D-13).

@ 67 S4 MERGE the current versions into the summary
origin mart.pr_publish_customers 0
value core.dim_customer.customer_id -> mart.customer_summary.customer_id identity
value core.dim_customer.full_name -> mart.customer_summary.full_name identity
value core.dim_customer.segment -> mart.customer_summary.segment identity
value core.dim_customer.region -> mart.customer_summary.region identity
filter core.dim_customer.is_current, core.dim_customer.valid_from -> mart.customer_summary
origin mart.pr_publish_customers 1
filter var:p_since -> mart.customer_summary
note USING's WHERE filters the MERGE (S3-03); ON is structural (D-5); p_since is a parameter, band 1.

@ 85 S5 one log row per region
origin mart.pr_publish_customers 1
value core.dim_customer.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.region identity
influence core.dim_customer.region -> mart.kpi_rollup.customers
filter core.dim_customer.is_current -> mart.kpi_rollup
note r.n is COUNT(*): no value source, but the loop query's GROUP BY governs it (influence); the loop's WHERE filters the write (B8 rule 4).
